  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1708.06950v2</id>
    <title>On Local laws for non-Hermitian random matrices and their products</title>
    <updated>2018-12-07T10:45:28Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.06950v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1708.06950v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>The aim of this paper is to prove a local version of the circular law for non-Hermitian random matrices and its generalization to the product of non-Hermitian random matrices under weak moment conditions. More precisely we assume that the entries $X_{jk}^{(q)}$ of non-Hermitian random matrices ${\bf X}^{(q)}, 1 \le j,k \le n, q = 1, \ldots, m, m \geq 1$ are i.i.d. r.v. with $\mathbb E X_{jk} =0, \mathbb E X_{jk}^2 = 1$ and $\mathbb E |X_{jk}|^{4+δ} &lt; \infty$ for some $δ&gt; 0$. It is shown that the local law holds on the optimal scale $n^{-1+2a}, a &gt; 0$, up to some logarithmic factor. We further develop a Stein type method to estimate the perturbation of the equations for the Stieltjes transform of the limiting distribution. We also generalize the recent results [Bourgade--Yau-Yin, 2014], [Tao--Vu, 2015] and [Nemish, 2017]. An extension to the case of non-i.i.d. entries is discussed.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math.SP" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
